@startuml sequence_frame_recording
title Frame Recording – Trainer → FrameRecorder → frames/{prefix}episode_NNNN.{ext}

actor "Researcher" as R
participant "EATrainer / CMAESTrainer /\nCoEvolutionTrainer / AgileRLTrainer" as T
participant "ExperimentLogger" as EL
participant "FrameRecorder" as FR
participant "UnifiedEvaluator\n(or _record_coevolution_rollout)" as UE
participant "PettingZooWrapper\n(render_mode='rgb_array')" as PZ
participant "imageio" as IO
participant "Filesystem\n<run_dir>/frames/" as FS

R -> T: train(config) where\nconfig.recording = RecordingConfig(\n  enabled=True, every_n_generations=None, fps=20,\n  fmt='mp4', max_frames_per_episode=None, max_dim=None, episode_prefix='')

== Recording setup (once per train()) ==
T -> EL: get_frame_recorder(\n  fps=cfg.fps, fmt=cfg.fmt,\n  max_frames_per_episode=cfg.max_frames_per_episode,\n  max_dim=cfg.max_dim,\n  episode_prefix=cfg.episode_prefix or 'train_')
EL -> FR: FrameRecorder(run_dir/'frames', fps,\n  fmt, max_frames_per_episode,\n  max_dim, episode_prefix='train_')
FR --> EL: recorder
EL --> T: recorder

note over T
  Cadence resolved by
  ``BaselineTrainer._resolve_recording_every_n``:
   • EA / CMA / CoEvo  default = 1
   • AgileRL           default = 10
  User-supplied value wins.
end note

== Champion rollout (every N generations) ==
loop generation g in 1..G  where g % every_n == 0
    T -> UE: evaluate(policy=champion,\n  env_name, num_episodes=1,\n  frame_recorder=recorder)
    UE -> PZ: reset()
    UE -> FR: start_episode()
    activate FR
    loop step
        UE -> PZ: render() → np.ndarray (H,W,3) uint8
        PZ --> UE: frame
        UE -> FR: add_frame(frame)
        UE -> PZ: step(actions)
    end
    UE -> FR: end_episode()
    FR -> IO: imwrite(frames/train_episode_{g:04d}.mp4, frames, fps)
    IO -> FS: write artefact
    deactivate FR
    UE --> T: EvaluationResult (discarded)
end

== Coevolution variant (heterogeneous policies) ==
note right of T
  CoEvolutionTrainer uses a custom
  ``_record_coevolution_rollout`` helper instead of
  ``UnifiedEvaluator.evaluate`` because evaluator broadcasts
  one policy to all agents but per-side obs sizes differ.
end note

== AgileRL variant (mid-training + final rollout) ==
note right of T
  AgileRLTrainer (MADDPG / MATD3 / IPPO /
  GroupedIPPO) records:
   • Mid-training champion rollouts at a configurable
     env-step cadence:
       - ``RecordingConfig.every_n_steps`` (explicit env steps)
         takes precedence;
       - else ``every_n_generations * params['learn_step']``
         is used as the env-step cadence;
       - both unset → no mid-training rollouts.
   • Exactly **one** end-of-training rollout, always emitted
     when ``recording.enabled`` is set, regardless of cadence.
  The same ``AgileRLPolicyWrapper`` is built **before**
  training and reused throughout — it holds a reference to
  the live agent so weight updates are visible at each
  recording call without rebuilding the wrapper.
  The recorder reuses the **same** ``ExperimentLogger``
  instance that writes ``metrics.csv`` / ``summary.json`` so
  ``frames/`` and the metric artefacts share a single
  ``run_dir``.
end note

== Cleanup ==
T -> EL: close()
note right of EL
  FrameRecorder has **no** close():
  artefacts are finalised inside
  each end_episode() call.
end note

@enduml
